      "title": "Participation is eligibility, not a promised payment",
      "narration": "Elena owns a participating whole life policy. Participating means it can share in the insurer's divisible surplus through policy dividends under its terms. A nonparticipating policy does not provide that participation. Neither label tells us whether the coverage is temporary or permanent. A declared dividend can reflect the insurer's experience with claims, investments and expenses. It is not a guaranteed future amount merely because dividends have been paid before. Keep the policy's contractual guarantees separate from a current dividend illustration. Under Maryland's rule, the insurer determines and apportions the stated surplus annually for participating policies. That duty does not guarantee a positive dividend every year.",
